                <h2>Affordability and Rent Burden Analysis</h2>
                <div class="summary-text">
                    Housing cost as a share of income is the single most actionable metric for policymakers. The charts below demonstrate the acute rent burden faced by cities globally, where housing costs consume a disproportionate share of local net salaries.
                </div>
                <div class="chart-row">
                    <div class="chart-container">{html_aff1}</div>
                    <div class="chart-container">{html_aff2}</div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="crisis-tier-profiling">
                <h2>Crisis Tier Profiling</h2>
                <div class="summary-text">
                    Cities are categorized into crisis tiers based on their economic stress levels. The profile below distinguishes high-crisis cities from affluent ones, showing severe disparities in purchasing power and affordability.
